272
00:23:56,040 --> 00:24:00,199
I'm also eager to see that devil.

273
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:26,479
Your greed is almost frightening me.

274
00:24:31,320 --> 00:24:33,199
What's this anger, Poena?

275
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:37,439
It's not Poena.

276
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:40,439
Halime.

277
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:51,879
What the hell are you talking about?

278
00:25:28,040 --> 00:25:31,879
Poena.

279
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:35,999
Poena.

280
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:18,759
Something happened.

281
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:20,919
Tell me.

282
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:22,759
What are you hiding from me?

283
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:25,679
I am not hiding anything.

284
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:27,079
I am just...

285
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:30,839
..eager for revenge.

286
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:35,199
Aunt...

287
00:27:21,760 --> 00:27:23,959
My Allah, what kind of treachery is this?

288
00:27:31,240 --> 00:27:34,239
I've never seen such
treacherous thing in my life.

289
00:27:50,680 --> 00:27:55,679
We bury our grudges in the
ground along with our enemies.

290
00:27:56,400 --> 00:28:02,799
But these devils have no respect
or mercy, even for the dead.

291
00:28:07,960 --> 00:28:12,759
Indeed we belong to Allah,
and indeed to Him we will return.

292
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:23,959
Never say that those martyred
in the cause of Allah are dead.

293
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:27,079
In fact, they are alive!

294
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:30,199
But you do not perceive it.

295
00:28:34,040 --> 00:28:35,679
I will make those who did this...

296
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:40,519
...learn the word of Allah in such a way that..

297
00:28:40,600 --> 00:28:44,639
...for every drop of blood shed by my martyrs...

298
00:28:45,360 --> 00:28:48,119
...I will make their blood flow like rivers.

299
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:52,839
Let's go, let's raid their outposts, my Bey.

300
00:28:52,840 --> 00:28:56,559
No, we can't move without precautions.

301
00:28:57,320 --> 00:28:58,879
First, we'll take precautions.

302
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:04,039
My Bey! My Bey!

303
00:29:06,560 --> 00:29:11,239
My Bey, we received important information
from the woodcutters in the forest.

304
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:17,159
My Bey, the infidels who left the outpost have
set a trap for the Turkmen unit on the road.

305
00:29:17,400 --> 00:29:19,599
Go to the tribe, take our martyrs.

306
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:21,879
As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

307
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:24,319
We are leaving.

308
00:29:59,800 --> 00:30:01,279
Sofia.

309
00:30:23,920 --> 00:30:26,599
What are you doing here?

310
00:30:26,800 --> 00:30:28,319
How can you ask me that?

311
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:32,279
Besides missing you?

312
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:39,479
I said... what are you doing here?

313
00:31:16,680 --> 00:31:20,919
Damn it.

314
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:25,919
Did the emperor send you for support?

315
00:31:26,760 --> 00:31:29,879
How could the emperor
find someone better than me?

316
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:34,679
And I thought to myself

317
00:31:35,760 --> 00:31:40,199
What could give me more
pleasure than taking Osman's head?

318
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:43,399
I thought it was seeing you.

319
00:31:43,840 --> 00:31:46,879
I volunteered for the mission.

320
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:49,679
To protect...

321
00:31:49,960 --> 00:31:52,879
..you and this beautiful Bursa.

322
00:31:58,120 --> 00:32:00,719
You dastards!

323
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:03,439
You treacherous infidels!

324
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:25,199
Dastard dogs!

325
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:31,479
Come on valiants!

326
00:32:31,480 --> 00:32:32,479
Attack!

327
00:32:32,480 --> 00:32:34,079
Allah is the Greatest!

328
00:32:36,520 --> 00:32:38,439
Koca Bey...

329
00:32:40,640 --> 00:32:43,079
Kill the infidels!

330
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:48,999
You infidels! Did you eat
barley instead of bread?

331
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:54,359
The leader of valiants my brother Hasan!

332
00:33:54,360 --> 00:33:57,479
You found this old man again, huh?

333
00:33:57,600 --> 00:33:58,959
Of course, I found him.

334
00:33:58,960 --> 00:34:02,159
There was a big mountain we leaned on.

335
00:34:02,320 --> 00:34:04,239
I thought I should go and find it.

336
00:34:33,239 --> 00:34:35,918
You say the mountains came together, huh?

337
00:34:37,840 --> 00:34:40,518
Come here, my brother.

338
00:34:41,840 --> 00:34:44,638
Thanks to the One Who let us come together!

339
00:34:46,400 --> 00:34:48,679
The ruler Osman Bey!

340
00:34:51,040 --> 00:34:55,478
So, the one who saved our lives
was the ruler of frontiers Osman Bey.

341
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:57,239
Thank you.

342
00:34:57,240 --> 00:35:00,719
Would Oghuz ever wait something
in return for another Oghuz' help?

343
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:03,199
Koca Bey spoke of you and your intentions.

344
00:35:03,200 --> 00:35:07,279
We still want the same thing. We
want to pledge our allegiance and unite.

345
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:12,279
But before that, I have
some important information.

346
00:35:12,520 --> 00:35:13,679
Tell me.

347
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:18,919
The deaths of Esenbike and
Sargun threw Olcaytu into hot flames.

348
00:35:19,240 --> 00:35:23,959
Those fires burned all
the Turkmen around Tabriz.

349
00:35:26,160 --> 00:35:27,519
Now..

350
00:35:27,960 --> 00:35:34,799
...the leader of the Mongol Noyans, Olcaytu's
most bloodthirsty sword, Orluk Kucar.

351
00:35:37,080 --> 00:35:39,599
He is coming to the frontiers as an envoy.

352
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:43,239
He will take the bodies of Esenbike and Sargun.

353
00:35:45,200 --> 00:35:47,279
Is Orluk Kucar..

354
00:35:48,800 --> 00:35:50,439
...coming as an envoy?

355
00:35:52,480 --> 00:35:58,839
My Bey, the Mongols have never sent someone
as an envoy in this position before.

356
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:04,599
So, there is a bigger
danger than the one we have.

357
00:36:06,840 --> 00:36:08,559
Alaeddin, Cerkutay.

358
00:36:09,400 --> 00:36:11,519
Go and welcome the envoy immediately.

359
00:36:12,240 --> 00:36:15,559
They need to be cautious as
they come to these borders.

360
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:18,359
-As you order my Bey.
-As you order my Bey.

361
00:36:18,360 --> 00:36:19,519
Aykurt.

362
00:36:23,080 --> 00:36:23,919
Thank you.

363
00:36:23,920 --> 00:36:27,039
The information you brought
is very important to us.

364
00:36:29,120 --> 00:36:30,519
Welcome to the borders.

365
00:36:30,520 --> 00:36:32,279
Thank you, Osman Bey.

366
00:36:49,760 --> 00:36:51,119
Sofia.

367
00:36:52,800 --> 00:36:55,919
I will never trust you, Glaudius.

368
00:36:55,920 --> 00:36:57,119
I've told you before.

369
00:36:57,120 --> 00:36:58,839
You...

370
00:36:59,840 --> 00:37:01,519
You betrayed my father.

371
00:37:01,520 --> 00:37:03,919
Your father was a very greedy man.

372
00:37:06,320 --> 00:37:07,879
Very greedy.

373
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:09,599
Shut up!

374
00:37:10,400 --> 00:37:14,279
And I am a man loyal to the emperor.

375
00:37:15,360 --> 00:37:16,799
Just like you.

376
00:37:18,600 --> 00:37:20,479
That's why you're still alive.

377
00:37:21,840 --> 00:37:24,319
That's why you're still here.

378
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:27,719
I'm still here too.

379
00:37:28,320 --> 00:37:30,079
Despite everything.

380
00:37:31,240 --> 00:37:34,679
Despite you betraying our love.

381
00:37:34,760 --> 00:37:38,239
I was never in love with you.

382
00:37:49,120 --> 00:37:50,319
Never?

383
00:37:50,320 --> 00:37:51,479
Never.

384
00:37:55,960 --> 00:37:58,639
The hearts you left broken behind...

385
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:01,999
...don't concern you, of course.

386
00:38:02,800 --> 00:38:04,479
You don't care.

387
00:38:07,640 --> 00:38:08,959
But Osman..

388
00:38:10,120 --> 00:38:12,039
We care about Osman.

389
00:38:13,640 --> 00:38:17,359
Olcaytu's son and daughter couldn't kill Osman.

390
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:20,639
But if we unite...

391
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:24,319
...we will kill that shepherd.

392
00:38:24,720 --> 00:38:28,239
What do you know about Osman?

393
00:38:32,160 --> 00:38:36,759
You know that outpost Osman wants to take back?

394
00:38:37,520 --> 00:38:40,159
I killed the men guarding it.

395
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:44,159
Then I went to the tribe.

396
00:38:45,280 --> 00:38:48,079
I looked into Osman's eyes...

397
00:38:48,160 --> 00:38:51,479
...and told him how his men were killed.

398
00:38:53,840 --> 00:38:57,359
I didn't tell him who did it, of
course, unnecessary information.

399
00:38:57,520 --> 00:38:59,039
I got to know Osman.

400
00:39:02,160 --> 00:39:04,639
I saw how his Alps lived.

401
00:39:07,200 --> 00:39:09,719
I looked into Osman's eyes.

402
00:39:11,200 --> 00:39:14,919
I saw his greed, his anger.

403
00:39:16,080 --> 00:39:17,159
What do you think?

404
00:39:19,360 --> 00:39:21,479
Do you think I know him a little?

405
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:23,039
I even...

406
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:28,519
I even know where Osman will attack first.

407
00:39:29,360 --> 00:39:32,679
He will attack the outpost to take revenge...

408
00:39:33,440 --> 00:39:35,839
...but I will be waiting for him there.

409
00:39:37,520 --> 00:39:39,039
Gladius..

410
00:39:41,920 --> 00:39:43,799
Where is your army?

411
00:39:44,240 --> 00:39:49,919
Half of my army is settled near the outpost
Osman wants to take back, waiting for my orders.

412
00:39:50,040 --> 00:39:51,879
What about the other half?

413
00:39:52,400 --> 00:39:55,359
The other half... Yes, it's important.

414
00:39:55,360 --> 00:40:01,279
Because they are my most trusted and loved men.

415
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:04,199
They are coming to me.

416
00:40:04,280 --> 00:40:06,999
They are coming here.

417
00:40:08,640 --> 00:40:10,759
I promise you, Sofia.

418
00:40:12,640 --> 00:40:15,119
Turks won't find a hole to hide.

419
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:17,639
They won't.

420
00:40:40,760 --> 00:40:43,279
Hasan Bey will stay with us.

421
00:40:43,280 --> 00:40:45,719
He came from far away.

422
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:49,359
There are Turkmen tribes around Tabriz.

423
00:40:49,520 --> 00:40:50,879
Welcome.

424
00:40:50,880 --> 00:40:52,039
Thank you.

425
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:53,599
Here, Hasan Bey.

426
00:41:01,240 --> 00:41:02,359
My Bey...

427
00:41:03,160 --> 00:41:04,999
You don't seem alright.

428
00:41:05,240 --> 00:41:06,959
Something must have happened.

429
00:41:07,040 --> 00:41:08,759
Koca Bey heard.

430
00:41:09,680 --> 00:41:11,959
Olcaytu's envoy will come...

431
00:41:12,080 --> 00:41:15,599
...to take Esenbike and Sargun's bodies.

432
00:41:17,560 --> 00:41:22,519
One trouble goes, another one comes.

433
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:52,759
What are you thinking
about, my gazelle-eyed one?

434
00:41:56,240 --> 00:41:58,039
It's been days...

435
00:41:58,040 --> 00:42:00,519
There's still no news from Meryem, my Bey.

436
00:42:01,200 --> 00:42:05,239
Don't worry. The Alps are searching everywhere.

437
00:42:06,160 --> 00:42:09,079
They will surely find a trace.

438
00:42:09,200 --> 00:42:13,519
Where would she go without informing
us? What if something happened to her?

439
00:42:13,520 --> 00:42:17,399
No, she is brave. Nothing
will happen to her, don't worry.

440
00:42:17,400 --> 00:42:20,359
She will come back safe and sound, God willing.

441
00:42:22,440 --> 00:42:24,599
May Allah not punish us for this but...

442
00:42:25,520 --> 00:42:30,439
Sometimes I think if we are being
tested with losing our loved ones.

443
00:42:30,720 --> 00:42:34,319
We lost Meryem before we
could come together with Halime.

444
00:42:34,320 --> 00:42:38,079
My Bala, there is good in everything.

445
00:42:38,120 --> 00:42:41,199
Aren't we the biggest witnesses of this?

446
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:42,439
Huh?

447
00:42:43,840 --> 00:42:48,439
If there were no separation, what
meaning would there be in reunion?

448
00:42:49,440 --> 00:42:53,039
But this reunion is very close.

449
00:42:54,200 --> 00:42:55,439
It is close.

450
00:42:57,360 --> 00:42:59,559
We got over many hardships...

451
00:43:01,040 --> 00:43:03,239
We got over many hardships...

452
00:43:03,440 --> 00:43:06,439
Now we are with our family in our tribe.

453
00:43:07,200 --> 00:43:09,239
I thought you were gone.

454
00:43:10,360 --> 00:43:13,079
I thought the breath I took was killing me.

455
00:43:13,760 --> 00:43:16,199
But then I found you again.

456
00:43:17,600 --> 00:43:19,359
Then we heard the good news...

457
00:43:20,280 --> 00:43:22,959
We found out that our daughter is alive.

458
00:43:23,320 --> 00:43:27,079
The fire that had gone out in
our hearts started burning again.

459
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:32,839
My Bala, this separation
will soon turn into reunion.

460
00:43:33,160 --> 00:43:37,159
We will reunite with Halime and Meryem.

461
00:43:38,120 --> 00:43:39,559
God willing.

462
00:43:41,440 --> 00:43:43,399
Speaking of Halime...

463
00:43:45,920 --> 00:43:48,439
I have something to tell you, Osman.

464
00:43:48,480 --> 00:43:49,719
Tell me.

465
00:44:25,520 --> 00:44:27,079
You are the horse of the tribe.

466
00:44:28,560 --> 00:44:29,639
Now...

467
00:44:31,440 --> 00:44:35,999
You will take this letter to
the tribe and be my confidant.

468
00:44:42,320 --> 00:44:43,479
Go, my girl.

469
00:44:56,960 --> 00:44:59,239
Go, my girl! Go!

470
00:45:00,600 --> 00:45:01,839
Go!

471
00:45:02,120 --> 00:45:03,879
Ruin Gladius' game!

472
00:45:16,040 --> 00:45:18,799
Stop the horse! Catch it!

473
00:45:38,040 --> 00:45:41,679
Calm down... Calm down...

474
00:45:42,840 --> 00:45:44,399
Ssh..
My girl...

475
00:45:52,280 --> 00:45:58,439
Let's see who you are sending this letter to.

476
00:45:59,720 --> 00:46:00,919
Soldiers!

477
00:46:18,480 --> 00:46:20,199
Priestess Lucia...

478
00:46:20,600 --> 00:46:23,439
...died before she could
tell us where Halime was.

479
00:46:23,720 --> 00:46:27,519
We just know her name and
that she is with Sofia, huh?

480
00:46:28,680 --> 00:46:29,839
Correct.

481
00:46:30,760 --> 00:46:33,479
But we are also looking for her in Bursa.

482
00:46:33,480 --> 00:46:35,039
In Bursa...

483
00:46:36,600 --> 00:46:41,959
You know, Holofira knows people in
Bursa... She knows an easy way to go there.

484
00:46:41,960 --> 00:46:44,919
So I say... I can go there secretly.

485
00:46:45,120 --> 00:46:49,839
With a few people, I will take our daughter
and come back before someone sees us, huh?

486
00:46:49,840 --> 00:46:52,999
No Bala. No.

487
00:46:53,520 --> 00:46:55,079
Sofia is in Bursa.

488
00:46:55,440 --> 00:46:57,519
She knows we are after her.

489
00:46:57,520 --> 00:47:00,799
That's why she controls every step we take.

490
00:47:00,840 --> 00:47:01,879
Besides...

491
00:47:03,960 --> 00:47:06,359
Finding Halime won't be that easy.

492
00:47:06,560 --> 00:47:10,279
We'll take precautions. We'll find a secret way.

493
00:47:12,520 --> 00:47:15,879
You are dreaming!
You are dreaming.

494
00:47:16,880 --> 00:47:18,599
Don't you know Sofia?

495
00:47:18,600 --> 00:47:20,279
Don't you know her games?

496
00:47:20,640 --> 00:47:24,879
Besides, if it were that easy, would I
leave my daughter in their hands, huh?

497
00:47:24,880 --> 00:47:26,719
I might be dreaming Osman...

498
00:47:27,000 --> 00:47:29,439
I am strong enough to chase that dream.

499
00:47:29,680 --> 00:47:32,799
If our daughter is there, I cannot stay here.

500
00:47:32,800 --> 00:47:34,079
Bala.

501
00:47:37,240 --> 00:47:39,159
I will not let this happen.

502
00:47:39,720 --> 00:47:40,879
No.

503
00:47:41,600 --> 00:47:43,359
Sofia is a demon.

504
00:47:44,880 --> 00:47:47,399
She is trying to attack
us by using our daughter.

505
00:47:47,760 --> 00:47:51,639
You might go to Bursa...

506
00:47:53,240 --> 00:47:55,359
But you'll never be able to leave.

507
00:47:56,880 --> 00:47:58,959
I cannot put you at risk.

508
00:48:02,360 --> 00:48:04,559
Don't, my Bala. Don't.

509
00:48:05,120 --> 00:48:07,479
This fire is our fire.

510
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:09,439
Your heart is in flames.

511
00:48:09,440 --> 00:48:10,999
Do you think mine is not?

512
00:48:11,000 --> 00:48:13,039
Do you think I am stone hearted?

513
00:48:15,240 --> 00:48:17,559
Since the day I found out about the truth...

514
00:48:18,720 --> 00:48:20,679
...I haven't been able to sleep.

515
00:48:22,720 --> 00:48:24,719
My gazelle eyed love.

516
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:27,079
They turned her against us.

517
00:48:27,080 --> 00:48:29,079
They made her her tribe's enemy.

518
00:48:29,160 --> 00:48:30,679
Think about it...

519
00:48:31,400 --> 00:48:33,319
Those gazelle eyes...

520
00:48:34,680 --> 00:48:37,479
...will look at us like we are her enemies.

521
00:48:38,040 --> 00:48:39,199
She will.

522
00:48:39,520 --> 00:48:41,719
If you are her mother, I am her father.

523
00:48:41,720 --> 00:48:43,239
I am her father.

524
00:48:48,840 --> 00:48:50,959
It hurts too much, Osman.

525
00:48:52,040 --> 00:48:54,159
This hope hurts even more.

526
00:48:54,360 --> 00:48:55,679
It tires us even more.

527
00:48:58,680 --> 00:49:00,159
Let me go.

528
00:49:00,640 --> 00:49:03,279
Please, let this longing end.

529
00:49:05,720 --> 00:49:07,759
I won't let you go there alone.

530
00:49:12,840 --> 00:49:14,679
Don't be upset.

531
00:49:15,760 --> 00:49:17,119
Don't worry.

532
00:49:17,800 --> 00:49:22,039
We will find Halime and Meryem. Don't worry.

533
00:49:22,040 --> 00:49:26,479
We will set out together. We will
fight together. We will find them.

534
00:49:28,400 --> 00:49:29,959
Don't worry.

535
00:49:49,840 --> 00:49:52,079
I told you many lies

536
00:49:52,280 --> 00:49:53,919
I made many mistakes.

537
00:49:54,280 --> 00:49:56,719
I have no courage to look at your faces.

538
00:49:56,840 --> 00:49:59,639
I am embarrassed. I didn't know.

539
00:50:00,760 --> 00:50:05,839
There is a truth that is hard
to believe and say for me.

540
00:50:05,840 --> 00:50:08,599
I am your daughter.

541
00:50:16,400 --> 00:50:18,199
Their daughter?!

542
00:50:28,080 --> 00:50:32,319
The Emperor sent Gladius
with a big army to Sofia for help.

543
00:50:32,840 --> 00:50:34,599
I wanted you to know this.

544
00:50:58,920 --> 00:51:00,119
Aunt..

545
00:51:08,640 --> 00:51:10,519
My daughter...

546
00:51:36,760 --> 00:51:38,239
Don't...

547
00:51:42,320 --> 00:51:43,199
Don't...

548
00:53:04,480 --> 00:53:09,999
They trust themselves so much
that they don't even guard the place.

549
00:53:11,000 --> 00:53:12,919
They just eat.

550
00:53:15,400 --> 00:53:17,519
They came to the frontiers...

551
00:53:18,160 --> 00:53:20,959
...they have thousands of enemies...

552
00:53:21,280 --> 00:53:22,319
..but..

553
00:53:22,760 --> 00:53:24,719
...they didn't take precautions, huh?

554
00:53:30,440 --> 00:53:35,999
There is something behind this.
-This is strange. -Dastard dogs.

555
00:53:36,640 --> 00:53:37,799
Come on.

556
00:53:38,120 --> 00:53:40,239
Let's get closer to them.

557
00:53:42,000 --> 00:53:43,079
Come on.

558
00:54:37,360 --> 00:54:39,719
Who are you, you demons?

559
00:54:45,240 --> 00:54:47,559
These are apparently the mute ones.

560
00:54:48,640 --> 00:54:51,119
They were trained with Chinese methods.

561
00:55:42,760 --> 00:55:44,119
Stop!

562
00:56:05,280 --> 00:56:07,239
Step back!

563
00:56:13,040 --> 00:56:18,199
You thought we did not take
measures and attacked us, huh?

564
00:56:19,360 --> 00:56:25,239
Who are you? Why are you here?
-We are Osman Bey's Alps.

565
00:56:32,160 --> 00:56:35,159
You are Osman Bey's Alps, huh?

566
00:56:43,360 --> 00:56:49,999
They thought you were not equal to
them, and they did not draw their swords...

567
00:56:50,040 --> 00:56:54,799
Or else, they would bury you all here.

568
00:56:55,440 --> 00:57:01,559
Taking our lives is not that easy, dear Envoy.

569
00:57:02,120 --> 00:57:03,999
Many like you...

570
00:57:04,880 --> 00:57:07,479
...died by our sword.

571
00:57:08,440 --> 00:57:10,319
You are in the lands of Kayi.

572
00:57:11,200 --> 00:57:13,039
Know your limits!

573
00:57:13,320 --> 00:57:14,959
You should be thankful...

574
00:57:15,680 --> 00:57:22,719
You should be thankful Osman's Alp... Or else...

575
00:57:23,160 --> 00:57:28,159
Or else? Or else what?
-Or else...

576
00:57:28,640 --> 00:57:31,519
I will kill you all here!

577
00:57:33,760 --> 00:57:38,679
No one could stand against
the great Ilkhanid Empire!

578
00:57:38,680 --> 00:57:40,839
Are you the ones to stand against it?

579
00:57:43,880 --> 00:57:45,319
Get ready.

580
00:57:48,680 --> 00:57:51,079
We are going to the Kayi tribe.

581
00:58:02,040 --> 00:58:04,159
We will accompany you.

582
00:58:11,120 --> 00:58:13,839
So you will lead the way for me, huh?

583
00:58:16,720 --> 00:58:21,079
You can only crawl behind me.

584
00:58:21,840 --> 00:58:24,399
Many Mongol envoys like you...

585
00:58:24,800 --> 00:58:26,679
...spoke like you.

586
00:58:27,840 --> 00:58:30,679
If you keep speaking like this...

587
00:58:31,120 --> 00:58:33,759
...you will die like they did.

588
00:58:33,760 --> 00:58:35,079
Know this!

589
00:58:50,600 --> 00:58:53,119
Those men beat us up, my Shahzade.

590
00:58:53,360 --> 00:58:55,359
They also made us drop our swords...

591
00:58:58,840 --> 00:59:00,959
We were caught unaware.

592
00:59:01,720 --> 00:59:07,999
But my Shahzade... I hope his
army is different than those few warriors!

593
00:59:08,600 --> 00:59:10,119
I hope so!

594
00:59:10,680 --> 00:59:12,159
I hope so!

595
00:59:15,120 --> 00:59:18,999
We will not give up, Cerkutay Bey. We won't.

596
00:59:20,320 --> 00:59:22,359
We will go after them.

597
00:59:23,000 --> 00:59:26,199
Come on now. Come on.

598
00:59:26,200 --> 00:59:35,079
You will find every child of
Osman in his family for me.

599
00:59:35,600 --> 00:59:39,039
I will take a girl...

600
00:59:39,440 --> 00:59:42,959
...and a boy from his family as a retaliation...

601
00:59:43,200 --> 00:59:45,679
...to Olcaytu Khan.

602
00:59:46,360 --> 00:59:50,239
If he does not give them,
we'll take them by force.

603
00:59:50,840 --> 00:59:52,599
Come on!

604
01:00:26,440 --> 01:00:30,119
So you decided that you've missed me. Come.

605
01:00:35,800 --> 01:00:38,239
The frontier lands are in a chaos.

606
01:00:38,320 --> 01:00:41,999
Olcaytu sent Mongols' most
bloodthirsty man Kucar...

607
01:00:42,320 --> 01:00:44,799
...to Osman as an envoy.

608
01:00:46,240 --> 01:00:48,639
Osman made a big mistake.

609
01:00:53,400 --> 01:00:56,999
He got himself into a big
trouble by killing those barbarians.

610
01:01:00,360 --> 01:01:01,919
I was the one..

611
01:01:02,760 --> 01:01:05,159
...who got Osman into this trouble.

612
01:01:05,640 --> 01:01:06,759
How?

613
01:01:10,360 --> 01:01:13,439
I killed Esenbike and Sargun...

614
01:01:13,760 --> 01:01:17,839
...and let Olcaytu attack Osman.

615
01:01:21,840 --> 01:01:28,199
You know... This mind of yours that is
overshadowed by your beauty... I admire it.

616
01:01:34,120 --> 01:01:35,319
I wonder..

617
01:01:35,680 --> 01:01:39,399
...if that same mind thought
about what Osman will do...

618
01:01:39,680 --> 01:01:42,159
...to us when he finds out about this?

619
01:01:42,920 --> 01:01:44,519
Are you afraid?

620
01:01:45,160 --> 01:01:46,319
Never..

621
01:01:48,880 --> 01:01:51,559
When I kill Osman tomorrow...

622
01:01:52,520 --> 01:01:56,479
...Bitinia will be all
clean. Every corner of it.

623
01:01:56,960 --> 01:01:58,959
Still..

624
01:01:59,360 --> 01:02:01,959
Get ready to meet Kucar.

625
01:02:02,560 --> 01:02:04,399
After Osman..

626
01:02:04,760 --> 01:02:06,879
...with us, in private.

627
01:02:07,440 --> 01:02:08,959
Yes, with us.

628
01:02:09,600 --> 01:02:14,759
He wants to have dinner together and talk.
-Good.

629
01:02:15,000 --> 01:02:18,239
I'll be there as well.
Someone needs to be there...

630
01:02:18,240 --> 01:02:20,799
...and control your anger.

631
01:02:42,080 --> 01:02:44,759
Attention! Osman Bey!

632
01:02:51,760 --> 01:02:54,159
Osman!

633
01:03:12,280 --> 01:03:14,359
Envoy Kucar, huh?

634
01:03:14,600 --> 01:03:16,759
We've been waiting for you.

635
01:03:18,160 --> 01:03:26,159
Before the Mongols reach their destination,
the wind always comes before their body.

636
01:03:28,680 --> 01:03:32,719
In your raids on your frontiers,
you learned who we were, Osman.

637
01:03:32,880 --> 01:03:36,399
Enemies must know each other well.

638
01:03:37,080 --> 01:03:39,599
The end of your arrival to the frontiers...

639
01:03:41,600 --> 01:03:44,559
...will be the proof of
your departure from here.

640
01:03:45,160 --> 01:03:52,119
The Khan of Khans, Olcaytu Khan who rules
the world is coming to the frontiers...

641
01:03:52,120 --> 01:03:54,599
..not to return this time.

642
01:03:56,000 --> 01:03:59,519
Of course, you can calm his anger.

643
01:03:59,840 --> 01:04:04,999
But for now, you will give
the bodies of Khanzades.

644
01:04:05,160 --> 01:04:07,039
Esenbike and Sargun.

645
01:04:07,800 --> 01:04:09,439
Here are their bodies.

646
01:04:26,680 --> 01:04:30,079
Give the order of our Khan to Osman.

647
01:04:57,320 --> 01:05:01,039
Only your knowing is not enough, Osman.

648
01:05:01,720 --> 01:05:07,639
Your Beys and your people must
also know the fate you have led them to.

649
01:05:10,640 --> 01:05:13,759
Our glorious Khan Olcaytu...

650
01:05:19,840 --> 01:05:23,439
...under one condition.

651
01:05:25,800 --> 01:05:31,999
In return for Esenbike
Hatun and Sargun, Osman...

652
01:05:33,040 --> 01:05:34,759
..will give..

653
01:05:37,000 --> 01:05:38,839
..a son and..

654
01:05:41,080 --> 01:05:43,759
...a daughter from his family...

655
01:05:44,440 --> 01:05:49,239
...to our great Khan Olcaytu.

656
01:05:59,560 --> 01:06:01,839
If he doesn't...

657
01:06:04,480 --> 01:06:05,839
Mongols...

658
01:06:06,920 --> 01:06:11,719
...let alone the people of Kayis...

659
01:06:11,960 --> 01:06:14,119
...let alone its Beys...

660
01:06:15,080 --> 01:06:21,799
...will kill even the birds and
sheep that live on these lands!

661
01:06:21,800 --> 01:06:24,399
Olcaytu's grandson and daughter...

662
01:06:27,320 --> 01:06:29,919
We did not take their lives.

663
01:06:30,960 --> 01:06:35,239
Do you have proof of this?

664
01:06:35,240 --> 01:06:39,599
I have no proof, and Allah is my only witness.

665
01:06:40,160 --> 01:06:41,319
But..

666
01:06:41,560 --> 01:06:44,199
...of course I will...

667
01:06:46,120 --> 01:06:47,799
...prove my word.

668
01:06:49,200 --> 01:06:50,319
Now..

669
01:06:52,200 --> 01:06:55,559
...go and tell your Khan.
Osman Bey...

670
01:06:56,840 --> 01:06:58,279
...never...

671
01:06:59,280 --> 01:07:01,359
...obeys the infidels.

672
01:07:06,600 --> 01:07:09,759
Then spend enough time
with your children, Osman.

673
01:07:12,400 --> 01:07:17,039
Your blood will flow like a
river to the frontier lands soon.

674
01:07:18,600 --> 01:07:19,919
Kayi...

675
01:07:20,160 --> 01:07:27,919
Bursa, and every piece of land
that is close to the frontiers...

676
01:07:28,280 --> 01:07:31,079
...will be ruled by Ilkhanids.

677
01:07:31,880 --> 01:07:35,479
Olcaytu will destroy you.

678
01:07:37,720 --> 01:07:38,999
Come on.

679
01:07:39,920 --> 01:07:41,399
We are leaving.

680
01:07:46,480 --> 01:07:48,799
Tell your Khan, envoy.

681
01:07:53,000 --> 01:07:56,719
...you want to take the lives of my children...

682
01:07:59,440 --> 01:08:03,199
...I will be waiting here to rip your heart out!

683
01:08:05,440 --> 01:08:06,479
Go now!

684
01:08:30,560 --> 01:08:31,799
My Beys!

685
01:08:33,640 --> 01:08:34,879
My Alps!

686
01:08:35,880 --> 01:08:37,037
We have never..

687
01:08:37,319 --> 01:08:42,879
...bowed before infidels, and
we will never bow! We saw...

688
01:08:43,200 --> 01:08:45,078
...death as shahada...

689
01:08:45,479 --> 01:08:47,599
...and grave as our positions!

690
01:08:48,479 --> 01:08:50,078
Now tell me..

691
01:08:50,760 --> 01:08:54,759
Are you with me to make Bursa and beyond...

692
01:08:55,160 --> 01:08:57,198
..Muslim lands?

693
01:08:57,200 --> 01:08:59,999
We are!

694
01:09:00,399 --> 01:09:01,719
Thank you.

695
01:09:02,160 --> 01:09:05,879
Thank you, live long.

696
01:09:07,040 --> 01:09:10,359
It's my order. Tomorrow

697
01:09:11,160 --> 01:09:14,881
We will take the lands
the infidels took from us

698
01:09:14,894 --> 01:09:18,399
and that are an obstacle
between us and Bursa.

699
01:09:19,439 --> 01:09:23,278
For the state, for the religion of Islam...

700
01:09:23,680 --> 01:09:27,639
...to spread the name of Turks in the world...

701
01:09:28,279 --> 01:09:34,959
...for the revenge of our
martyrs and veterans, I swear...

702
01:09:34,960 --> 01:09:37,238
...we will never give up on battle!

703
01:09:39,359 --> 01:09:40,999
Allah is the Greatest!

704
01:09:42,000 --> 01:09:43,479
Allah is the Greatest!

705
01:10:00,800 --> 01:10:02,079
God..

706
01:10:05,400 --> 01:10:08,279
Show me the right way once again.

707
01:10:11,240 --> 01:10:14,799
I committed sins that can never be forgiven.

708
01:10:17,720 --> 01:10:19,839
Welcome, my little bird.

709
01:10:21,440 --> 01:10:23,519
Why didn't you go to sleep?

710
01:10:27,600 --> 01:10:29,159
I had a nightmare.

711
01:10:37,440 --> 01:10:39,239
It's good that you are here.

712
01:10:41,840 --> 01:10:45,559
There is something important
that I want to talk to you about.

713
01:10:48,440 --> 01:10:49,719
Maybe...

714
01:10:50,480 --> 01:10:53,239
You will get really mad at me... Maybe...

715
01:10:54,120 --> 01:10:57,319
...you will hate me...

716
01:11:00,440 --> 01:11:01,479
But...

717
01:11:03,560 --> 01:11:06,239
I cannot carry this secret anymore.

718
01:11:08,480 --> 01:11:10,159
What do you mean?

719
01:11:11,760 --> 01:11:12,959
Aunt?

720
01:11:28,040 --> 01:11:30,999
I always wanted to have a child.

721
01:11:32,360 --> 01:11:34,279
I could not give birth to a child...

722
01:11:34,640 --> 01:11:38,199
...who would carry the blood of Master Yannis.

723
01:11:39,520 --> 01:11:41,359
My biggest enemy...

724
01:11:42,680 --> 01:11:46,519
...caused such a deep wound in a battle that...

725
01:11:46,520 --> 01:11:48,919
...he stole my future.

726
01:11:50,400 --> 01:11:53,839
I will never have a child.

727
01:11:57,280 --> 01:11:59,439
I was in great pain. Poena.

728
01:12:00,480 --> 01:12:05,639
My dreams were stolen from me. I
couldn't have lived without a child.

729
01:12:06,840 --> 01:12:08,199
And that day...

730
01:12:09,400 --> 01:12:12,159
...the last piece of innocence...

731
01:12:14,240 --> 01:12:19,279
...in me was buried under the ground. 
-No.

732
01:12:20,640 --> 01:12:21,759
And I...

733
01:12:28,080 --> 01:12:32,439
...kidnapped the daughter of my
enemy who was the reason of this.

734
01:12:38,360 --> 01:12:40,439
What are you saying?

735
01:12:43,160 --> 01:12:44,319
You..

736
01:12:46,760 --> 01:12:53,319
Even if you carry their
blood, you are my daughter.

737
01:12:55,440 --> 01:12:58,399
I was in hell before you.

738
01:12:59,360 --> 01:13:03,719
I was in a dark cold dungeon, but you...

739
01:13:05,800 --> 01:13:08,919
You were a light in that dungeon.

740
01:13:11,680 --> 01:13:14,319
You were the reason for me to live.

741
01:13:21,440 --> 01:13:22,679
But this..

742
01:13:25,000 --> 01:13:28,559
...does not change what I did to you.
It cannot make you forgive it.

743
01:13:35,000 --> 01:13:37,239
But maybe, if you kill me...

744
01:13:41,080 --> 01:13:44,119
...you can relieve...

745
01:13:45,400 --> 01:13:46,679
..your heart.

746
01:14:00,200 --> 01:14:01,759
Kill me now.

747
01:14:05,800 --> 01:14:07,239
Kill me.

748
01:14:12,280 --> 01:14:19,519
You stole my life from me!

749
01:14:19,920 --> 01:14:23,599
Was it for revenge? Revenge!

750
01:14:24,880 --> 01:14:26,359
For revenge..

751
01:14:31,680 --> 01:14:33,559
You took..

752
01:14:33,800 --> 01:14:35,479
...everything from me.

753
01:14:36,680 --> 01:14:42,239
You took everything from me!
-My feelings are real.

754
01:14:43,160 --> 01:14:44,199
You are lying!

755
01:14:45,000 --> 01:14:46,759
My feelings...

756
01:14:47,040 --> 01:14:49,039
...were real, Poena. -No!

757
01:14:52,640 --> 01:14:54,879
You are my daughter!

758
01:14:57,840 --> 01:15:00,039
You are a liar!

759
01:15:00,640 --> 01:15:05,039
You are lying! You are lying!

760
01:15:07,560 --> 01:15:09,679
I can never forgive you!

761
01:15:10,680 --> 01:15:11,919
I will never..

762
01:15:12,320 --> 01:15:14,159
I will never forgive you!

763
01:15:14,360 --> 01:15:17,759
I will never ever forgive you!

764
01:15:25,640 --> 01:15:26,879
Aunt..

765
01:15:33,440 --> 01:15:35,239
You coughed up blood.

766
01:15:39,120 --> 01:15:42,999
Neither God nor you will never forgive me.

767
01:15:49,800 --> 01:15:50,919
And I...

768
01:15:52,600 --> 01:15:57,119
...dreamt of a long life with you
but God will not let that come true.

769
01:16:06,280 --> 01:16:08,279
He already punished me.

770
01:16:10,960 --> 01:16:13,639
I am dying. Poena.

771
01:16:16,160 --> 01:16:18,799
Doctors said I am so sick that...

772
01:16:19,480 --> 01:16:21,559
...I won't even make it to this summer.

773
01:16:32,240 --> 01:16:33,399
Beys...

774
01:16:33,920 --> 01:16:35,399
...all together...

775
01:16:35,800 --> 01:16:39,319
...we will move from both sides. On one side...

776
01:16:39,680 --> 01:16:42,239
...the Byzantium outpost...

777
01:16:42,480 --> 01:16:47,359
...on this hill that is on our
weakest spot and on the other side...

778
01:16:48,960 --> 01:16:51,679
...Gladius' support unit.

779
01:16:53,360 --> 01:16:56,559
Both duties are quite tough, Osman Bey.

780
01:16:56,840 --> 01:17:01,759
So, what is our plan? -Yes, yes.

781
01:17:02,880 --> 01:17:06,519
We will plan everything. Don't worry.

782
01:17:06,960 --> 01:17:08,079
Now...

783
01:17:08,840 --> 01:17:10,199
Orhan, Alaeddin.

784
01:17:10,920 --> 01:17:12,839
Boran, Cerkutay.

785
01:17:13,240 --> 01:17:14,559
Now you..

786
01:17:15,440 --> 01:17:18,919
...will raid the Byzantium outpost together.

787
01:17:19,120 --> 01:17:24,719
You will attack from both sides.
And you will sneak in from here.

788
01:17:25,040 --> 01:17:26,719
Whoever stands..

789
01:17:27,560 --> 01:17:29,599
...on this spot...

790
01:17:30,440 --> 01:17:32,159
...you will turn that place...

791
01:17:33,240 --> 01:17:38,159
...into their graves. As you order, my Bey.

792
01:17:39,480 --> 01:17:40,559
My Bey...

793
01:17:41,200 --> 01:17:44,079
Sure, it is not easy to raid the outpost.

794
01:17:44,360 --> 01:17:48,159
But defeating the support
unit... It's much more difficult.

795
01:17:48,560 --> 01:17:54,279
Therefore, either my brother or I should
come with you my Bey. Those dogs...

796
01:17:54,480 --> 01:17:57,039
...will bring many men along.
-No.

797
01:17:57,680 --> 01:17:59,359
I made my decision.

798
01:18:01,200 --> 01:18:02,439
Koca Bey...

799
01:18:03,720 --> 01:18:05,399
And Hasan Bey.

800
01:18:06,680 --> 01:18:08,679
We'll go there together.

801
01:18:09,680 --> 01:18:10,919
Beys...

802
01:18:11,840 --> 01:18:14,759
...and you will carry out...

803
01:18:15,440 --> 01:18:19,079
...this duty together.
As you order my Bey.

804
01:18:19,080 --> 01:18:20,519
As you order, my Bey

805
01:18:21,440 --> 01:18:23,359
But don't forget.

806
01:18:23,560 --> 01:18:24,919
There is...

807
01:18:25,160 --> 01:18:29,399
...of course shahada on this
way. We might become veterans.

808
01:18:29,640 --> 01:18:30,679
But..

809
01:18:31,400 --> 01:18:33,319
...those who do not live for freedom..

810
01:18:33,920 --> 01:18:35,839
...die in captivity.

811
01:18:36,480 --> 01:18:37,879
Come on now.

812
01:18:39,800 --> 01:18:44,479
-May our war be blessed.
-Aameen. -Aameen.

813
01:18:48,760 --> 01:18:50,719
We heard that...

814
01:18:51,720 --> 01:18:55,919
...you sent the bodies of Esenbike and Sargun...

815
01:18:55,920 --> 01:18:59,599
...to Olcaytu Khan but
you didn't ask for anything...

816
01:19:00,520 --> 01:19:04,199
...from Osman in return.

817
01:19:05,160 --> 01:19:06,999
What they did...

818
01:19:08,800 --> 01:19:10,879
...is disrespectful to you.

819
01:19:26,480 --> 01:19:27,519
You..

820
01:19:28,200 --> 01:19:31,279
...don't worry about Osman, Hatun.

821
01:19:33,520 --> 01:19:36,079
Osman..

822
01:19:36,320 --> 01:19:39,279
...is living his last days.

823
01:19:42,200 --> 01:19:47,119
He will see the furor of Ilkhanid Empire soon.

824
01:19:50,760 --> 01:19:53,357
No one has ever had
the power to stand against

825
01:19:53,369 --> 01:19:56,199
Olcaytu Khan. Osman
won't be able to do so as well.

826
01:19:56,680 --> 01:19:57,759
But...

827
01:19:58,200 --> 01:20:01,119
...there is something we wonder...

828
01:20:02,280 --> 01:20:05,679
When will your armies come to the frontiers?

829
01:20:12,800 --> 01:20:15,479
We never leave our revenge half-finished.

830
01:20:18,480 --> 01:20:20,999
Every creature that stands in our way...

831
01:20:21,160 --> 01:20:25,559
...and that does not bow to us...

832
01:20:27,280 --> 01:20:29,119
...will die and perish.

833
01:20:39,040 --> 01:20:40,559
Now..

834
01:20:41,920 --> 01:20:43,239
I have..

835
01:20:45,480 --> 01:20:47,399
..an offer for you.

836
01:20:53,040 --> 01:20:55,159
The Khan of Khans...

837
01:20:56,280 --> 01:20:59,839
...my glorious Khan Olcaytu Khan...

838
01:21:00,400 --> 01:21:06,119
...wants to make an alliance with you.

839
01:21:10,800 --> 01:21:12,759
The things you say...

840
01:21:13,840 --> 01:21:15,959
...sound like music to me.

841
01:21:16,800 --> 01:21:17,959
Sure..

842
01:21:18,720 --> 01:21:20,479
Osman's enemies...

843
01:21:20,800 --> 01:21:22,599
...are our friends.

844
01:21:26,360 --> 01:21:28,399
Great Roman Empire...

845
01:21:29,200 --> 01:21:34,287
...will make an alliance with
Olcaytu Khan. Don't worry.

846
01:21:34,299 --> 01:21:35,999
Excellent!

847
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:37,879
I am glad!

848
01:21:38,680 --> 01:21:41,399
It made me really happy.

849
01:21:41,880 --> 01:21:43,079
We..

850
01:21:45,640 --> 01:21:48,279
...will stand next to you in the war...

851
01:21:48,800 --> 01:21:51,559
...you will wage against Turks, Kucar.

852
01:22:00,320 --> 01:22:03,119
Not next to us, Hatun.

853
01:22:06,080 --> 01:22:09,879
At our service.

854
01:22:10,960 --> 01:22:11,999
Pour some.

855
01:22:20,880 --> 01:22:23,279
What do you mean?

856
01:22:25,080 --> 01:22:27,759
Ilkhanid Empire...

857
01:22:28,840 --> 01:22:31,959
...is not looking for friends.

858
01:22:32,640 --> 01:22:36,799
We just want servants...

859
01:22:37,280 --> 01:22:44,079
...who will bow their heads, tie
their hands and kneel before us!

860
01:22:49,080 --> 01:22:53,359
You will give Bursa to us.

861
01:22:53,720 --> 01:22:55,119
Pour some.

862
01:23:06,000 --> 01:23:08,359
What does that mean?

863
01:23:10,160 --> 01:23:12,479
Our target

864
01:23:13,720 --> 01:23:17,639
...is having all the lands in the West.

865
01:23:30,240 --> 01:23:32,999
If you do not bow...

866
01:23:33,920 --> 01:23:38,039
When my glorious ruler Olcaytu comes...

867
01:23:42,520 --> 01:23:44,599
...he will first destroy Osman...

868
01:23:46,760 --> 01:23:51,159
...then these palaces that you trust so much..

869
01:23:52,000 --> 01:23:56,999
...and the walls here and there.

870
01:24:02,080 --> 01:24:04,439
Holy Roman Empire...

871
01:24:04,440 --> 01:24:08,399
...will never bow to anyone! Know that!

872
01:24:12,120 --> 01:24:14,679
It will. It will.

873
01:24:16,200 --> 01:24:19,719
My glorious ruler is so generous that...

874
01:24:20,640 --> 01:24:24,639
...he will let you practice your religion.

875
01:24:24,640 --> 01:24:29,959
You can also trade. Don't
worry about these two things.

876
01:24:30,600 --> 01:24:34,319
And you can also...

877
01:24:34,600 --> 01:24:36,799
...protect your positions.

878
01:24:38,440 --> 01:24:40,839
You will pay us the tax we determine...

879
01:24:41,240 --> 01:24:47,559
...to the Ilkhanid governor
we will appoint for Bursa.

880
01:24:48,040 --> 01:24:53,439
Do you think we are the same
as those looter tribe Beys?

881
01:24:56,160 --> 01:24:57,439
We..

882
01:24:58,720 --> 01:25:01,519
...crush anyone..

883
01:25:01,720 --> 01:25:05,239
...who stands in our way and does not bow.

884
01:25:09,520 --> 01:25:12,439
I am giving you two days.

885
01:25:14,760 --> 01:25:16,879
Think.

886
01:25:17,520 --> 01:25:18,959
And decide.

887
01:25:24,200 --> 01:25:26,879
Will you choose living?

888
01:25:32,720 --> 01:25:34,039
Or dying?

889
01:25:53,720 --> 01:25:56,719
By killing Esenbike and Sargun...

890
01:25:57,120 --> 01:26:00,519
...you put us into a very
difficult position, Sofia.

891
01:26:01,080 --> 01:26:06,519
Now we are not only facing
Osman but also the Ilkhanid state.

892
01:26:08,720 --> 01:26:11,439
As long as I am alive...

893
01:26:11,880 --> 01:26:16,119
...I will never bow down to anyone! And I...

894
01:26:23,160 --> 01:26:24,479
Never!

895
01:26:55,560 --> 01:26:56,879
Stop!

896
01:26:59,240 --> 01:27:01,119
Don't take another step!

897
01:27:03,800 --> 01:27:04,999
That's Osman!

898
01:27:06,120 --> 01:27:10,639
If you take another step, you
will let Azrael take your life.

899
01:27:10,640 --> 01:27:12,399
Do you think you can

900
01:27:12,400 --> 01:27:15,199
...defeat us alone, Osman?

901
01:27:15,560 --> 01:27:18,919
I will skin you out and make it
a sheath for my sword, Osman.

902
01:27:18,960 --> 01:27:22,759
I will drag your miserable body behind my horse.

903
01:27:39,680 --> 01:27:42,319
Look at us, you dastards!

904
01:27:42,600 --> 01:27:44,799
Wolves are not alone!

905
01:27:45,200 --> 01:27:48,479
Wolves are not fools!

906
01:27:48,480 --> 01:27:52,359
Many have come to turn
the frontiers into my grave..

907
01:27:52,360 --> 01:27:58,199
But they all died. Now,
it's time for you to suffer.

908
01:27:59,520 --> 01:28:00,559
Come on.

909
01:28:04,000 --> 01:28:05,959
-Alps!
-Allah is the greatest!

910
01:28:15,440 --> 01:28:19,049
Allah is Eternal!

911
01:28:53,240 --> 01:28:57,119
I have the left wing.
-I have the left wing, brother.

912
01:28:57,880 --> 01:28:59,039
Come on, alps.

913
01:28:59,440 --> 01:29:01,479
We'll sneak in silently.

914
01:29:02,920 --> 01:29:04,599
Come on Cerkutay Bey.

915
01:29:18,840 --> 01:29:20,239
O Allah!

916
01:29:44,640 --> 01:29:48,519
Draw your swords! Allah is the Greatest!

917
01:30:00,600 --> 01:30:02,439
Allah is the Greatest!

918
01:30:05,360 --> 01:30:08,439
Don't let any of them survive, Alps!

919
01:30:49,840 --> 01:30:52,159
Come on Alps! Come on!

920
01:31:00,320 --> 01:31:04,119
They are weaker now Alps! Attack them!

921
01:31:08,560 --> 01:31:12,079
It is falling my Shahzade!
The outpost is falling!

922
01:31:12,080 --> 01:31:14,599
The victory is ours God willing!

923
01:31:49,400 --> 01:31:51,319
Throw!

924
01:31:59,480 --> 01:32:02,399
Alps! Come back!

925
01:32:14,680 --> 01:32:19,359
Kayis! I brought hell to you!

926
01:32:30,800 --> 01:32:31,839
Walk!

927
01:34:12,920 --> 01:34:17,479
Come on Alps! Allah is the Greatest!

928
01:34:19,840 --> 01:34:24,119
My Shahzade! My Shahzade!

929
01:34:24,120 --> 01:34:26,999
We need to retreat! We are losing too many Alps!

930
01:34:27,000 --> 01:34:30,879
They are all becoming martyrs!
-My Allah, help us!

931
01:34:30,880 --> 01:34:35,119
Alps! We are retreating!
Come on! Or we will all die here!

932
01:34:35,120 --> 01:34:39,159
Come on! We will die here! Come on!

933
01:34:39,960 --> 01:34:42,519
Retreat! Retreat!

934
01:34:54,200 --> 01:34:56,679
-Come on!
-Alaeddin!

935
01:34:57,720 --> 01:35:00,239
No, Alaeddin!

936
01:35:02,160 --> 01:35:04,159
Come on!

937
01:35:04,160 --> 01:35:06,106
Alaeddin! What are you doing?

938
01:35:06,118 --> 01:35:08,279
Come on! Come on Cerkutay Bey!

939
01:35:08,280 --> 01:35:11,359
Come on! -Cerkutay Bey!
-Come on brothers!

940
01:35:16,960 --> 01:35:19,319
Alaeddin! Alaeddin!

941
01:35:19,880 --> 01:35:23,239
What are you doing?!

942
01:35:23,680 --> 01:35:26,159
Alaeddin!

943
01:35:31,160 --> 01:35:33,830
Come on! Come on!

944
01:35:33,830 --> 01:35:35,459
Alaeddin!

945
01:35:46,680 --> 01:35:49,439
Come at me.

946
01:35:57,720 --> 01:35:59,959
You weak infidel...

947
01:35:59,960 --> 01:36:02,559
You thin, dry stick!

948
01:36:02,640 --> 01:36:07,439
Are you going to fight with the great
plane tree, huh? Come on, make your move!

949
01:36:07,440 --> 01:36:09,879
Make your move and I will rip your heart out!

950
01:36:54,440 --> 01:36:56,359
Die Osman!

951
01:37:10,080 --> 01:37:13,159
Were you going to kill me with this sword, huh?

952
01:37:21,760 --> 01:37:24,079
You dastard dog!

953
01:37:48,000 --> 01:37:51,467
My Bey... That coward is
running away, I'll go after him.

954
01:37:51,479 --> 01:37:52,639
Stop!

955
01:37:52,640 --> 01:37:56,039
Hasan Bey... Don't tire yourself, let him go!

956
01:38:01,600 --> 01:38:03,159
Thank Allah.

957
01:38:04,160 --> 01:38:07,799
Don't, my Osman Bey. Are we
going to let that dastard run away?

958
01:38:07,800 --> 01:38:09,239
No.

959
01:38:09,520 --> 01:38:11,159
Let him go.

960
01:38:11,640 --> 01:38:14,319
Don't you want our victory to be heard, huh?

961
01:38:14,880 --> 01:38:16,199
Let him go now.

962
01:38:16,720 --> 01:38:20,439
Let him tell his owner
everything. Let him tell Gladius...

963
01:38:20,440 --> 01:38:24,919
...how they lost.

964
01:38:24,920 --> 01:38:28,999
-There is a pile of treasure in the cart, my Bey.
-Okay.

965
01:38:29,600 --> 01:38:35,119
Okay. So, the sword that
the infidels draw against us...

966
01:38:35,120 --> 01:38:38,279
...will always be driven into their hearts.

967
01:38:39,200 --> 01:38:41,039
Thanks to Allah.

968
01:38:41,600 --> 01:38:43,525
We did not let them win.

969
01:38:43,537 --> 01:38:46,119
-Thank Allah.
-Thank Allah.

970
01:38:46,120 --> 01:38:47,359
Come on now.

971
01:38:47,840 --> 01:38:49,199
Take these.

972
01:38:49,560 --> 01:38:51,159
We are going to the tribe.

973
01:38:51,360 --> 01:38:53,679
Bring the horses.
-As you order, my Bey.

974
01:39:03,880 --> 01:39:06,879
We cannot resist now. They
are coming at us like dogs!

975
01:39:06,880 --> 01:39:09,479
We need to retreat! -Come!

976
01:39:17,520 --> 01:39:20,559
We will resist, Boran Bey! We will resist!

977
01:39:20,560 --> 01:39:23,879
My Shahzade, they left us alone.
We need to retreat, my Shahzade!

978
01:39:23,880 --> 01:39:25,119
We will resist!

979
01:39:28,520 --> 01:39:33,719
Hang on, Alps! Allah is with us! Hang on!

980
01:39:47,600 --> 01:39:48,719
Yusuf!

981
01:40:03,720 --> 01:40:04,919
Yusuf!

982
01:40:13,520 --> 01:40:17,719
My Shahzade, we need to retreat, come on!
-Boran Bey, our martyrs...

983
01:40:17,720 --> 01:40:21,959
...our Alps! We cannot leave
them here! We lost many Alps!

984
01:40:21,960 --> 01:40:23,919
We have many martyrs!

985
01:40:24,960 --> 01:40:26,199
Yusuf.

986
01:40:26,920 --> 01:40:29,159
Yusuf! -My Shahzade! -Yusuf!

987
01:40:29,160 --> 01:40:31,719
My Shahzade, Yusuf was martyred.

988
01:40:33,040 --> 01:40:36,879
My Shahzade, don't worry.
We won't leave our martyrs here.

989
01:40:36,880 --> 01:40:40,919
But not now. We need to retreat, my Shahzade.
-Yusuf. -Come on.

990
01:40:40,920 --> 01:40:45,679
Alaeddin, I will make you regret
this! I will make you regret this!

991
01:40:45,880 --> 01:40:52,559
-We are retreating! Come on! Brother!
-Cowards ran away! The fools are here!

992
01:40:52,560 --> 01:40:54,199
Kill them all!

993
01:41:05,840 --> 01:41:09,359
Come on! Come on!

994
01:41:10,040 --> 01:41:12,839
Run, you dogs! Run!

995
01:41:12,840 --> 01:41:19,679
You will never be able to
take this outpost! Never!

996
01:41:30,240 --> 01:41:32,679
He is still alive. Commander Gladius.

997
01:41:37,880 --> 01:41:41,439
Coward Osman did not come here.

998
01:41:42,280 --> 01:41:45,079
He sent his looter Shahzades, right?

999
01:41:49,000 --> 01:41:51,279
You will lose.

1000
01:41:53,360 --> 01:41:54,919
You will lose.

1001
01:41:55,680 --> 01:41:58,079
I will become a martyr.

1002
01:41:58,880 --> 01:42:02,119
-You will lose. 
-I will lose?

1003
01:42:05,120 --> 01:42:08,039
You are the one fighting
for your life on the ground.

1004
01:42:08,160 --> 01:42:09,359
Not me.

1005
01:42:14,280 --> 01:42:20,759
You are a dastard dog.
You are destined to lose.

1006
01:42:20,760 --> 01:42:24,999
You are too courageous
for a man who is about to die.

1007
01:42:25,960 --> 01:42:29,679
Then while you are
approaching hell step by step..

1008
01:42:30,640 --> 01:42:34,759
...take the things you believe. Hold on to them.

1009
01:42:34,760 --> 01:42:36,679
Because you will need them.

1010
01:42:40,160 --> 01:42:45,239
I bear witness that there is none
worthy of worship except Allah...

1011
01:42:46,640 --> 01:42:50,319
...and I bear witness that Muhammad
is His servant and Messenger.

1012
01:43:00,720 --> 01:43:03,039
Take this dead body to Osman.

1013
01:43:05,600 --> 01:43:07,079
With my best intentions.

1014
01:43:13,960 --> 01:43:16,479
Kanyumaz! Find a carrier now!

1015
01:43:16,520 --> 01:43:20,399
We will take the injured to the tribe! Hurry!
-As you order, my Shahzade!

1016
01:43:20,400 --> 01:43:23,959
My Shahzade! -Come.

1017
01:43:25,360 --> 01:43:30,239
You'll be alright. You'll be alright. I am here.

1018
01:43:31,560 --> 01:43:38,719
You'll be alright. You'll be
alright. Everything will be alright.

1019
01:43:38,920 --> 01:43:40,319
You'll be alright. Come on.

1020
01:43:43,880 --> 01:43:47,239
I don't understand why Alaeddin Bey retreated.

1021
01:43:47,240 --> 01:43:49,199
All those Alps and martyrs.

1022
01:43:52,600 --> 01:43:54,159
Alaeddin!

1023
01:43:55,480 --> 01:43:58,839
Brother... Brother... Here.

1024
01:43:59,640 --> 01:44:00,959
Alaeddin!

1025
01:44:03,880 --> 01:44:05,279
Brother!

1026
01:44:08,840 --> 01:44:14,039
What do you think you are doing, huh? Why
did you retreat in the middle of the battle?

1027
01:44:14,080 --> 01:44:17,999
Why did you leave us alone
in the hands of infidels?!

1028
01:44:18,160 --> 01:44:19,559
What was I supposed to do?

1029
01:44:19,560 --> 01:44:21,991
If I hadn't retreated, all
the Alps would have died.

1030
01:44:22,003 --> 01:44:22,879
They should have!

1031
01:44:22,880 --> 01:44:27,999
We would all die there with our
honour there if necessary! But you...

1032
01:44:28,000 --> 01:44:32,479
But you should have let me
know before doing such a thing!

1033
01:44:32,800 --> 01:44:35,279
What do you think happened there?

1034
01:44:36,280 --> 01:44:39,759
Do you know what happened there? The infidels...

1035
01:44:39,760 --> 01:44:44,759
They all attacked us!
For our cause...

1036
01:44:45,040 --> 01:44:49,039
The Alps who fought for
our cause became martyrs!

1037
01:44:49,040 --> 01:44:52,239
We left our martyrs there!

1038
01:44:57,280 --> 01:45:00,319
Alaeddin. Look at my face!

1039
01:45:00,600 --> 01:45:02,039
Yusuf.

1040
01:45:02,880 --> 01:45:04,759
Yusuf and many other Alps...

1041
01:45:05,560 --> 01:45:07,639
They all became martyrs Alaeddin.

1042
01:45:08,080 --> 01:45:09,439
All of them!

1043
01:45:15,080 --> 01:45:16,359
Brother..

1044
01:45:18,600 --> 01:45:20,599
Look, you are saying wrong things...

1045
01:45:21,360 --> 01:45:23,759
-I did what was right. 
-Shut up!

1046
01:45:24,920 --> 01:45:26,319
Shut up!

1047
01:45:28,800 --> 01:45:30,239
Tell me now!

1048
01:45:30,920 --> 01:45:34,559
How are we going to take our
martyrs from there, Alaeddin?

1049
01:45:34,600 --> 01:45:36,679
Tell me now, Alaeddin!

1050
01:45:36,680 --> 01:45:40,719
How are we going to look at
Osman Bey's face, Alaeddin?!

1051
01:45:41,120 --> 01:45:43,159
We could have gained a victory.

1052
01:45:43,160 --> 01:45:45,519
We lost because you retreated!

1053
01:45:45,520 --> 01:45:47,969
How can you be so arrogant, Orhan Bey?

1054
01:45:48,000 --> 01:45:53,199
You are blinded by your
ambition for victory! This is battle!

1055
01:45:53,240 --> 01:45:55,839
Retreating is as normal as attacking!

1056
01:45:55,840 --> 01:45:59,199
I retreated to protect
the lives of our valiants!

1057
01:46:00,200 --> 01:46:01,599
The right thing...

1058
01:46:02,720 --> 01:46:07,399
...was to retreat.
-Retreat? That was not retreating, brother.

1059
01:46:07,640 --> 01:46:09,839
That was running away, Cerkutay.

1060
01:46:14,120 --> 01:46:15,679
What will happen now?

1061
01:46:16,720 --> 01:46:19,239
Let me tell you what will happen

1062
01:46:19,720 --> 01:46:22,119
When we go back to the tribe...

1063
01:46:22,880 --> 01:46:25,359
You will answer for..

1064
01:46:25,720 --> 01:46:27,839
...all the things you did...

1065
01:46:28,080 --> 01:46:30,479
...before my father!

1066
01:46:32,160 --> 01:46:36,359
Enough! I had enough! Why do
you think you are right every time?!

1067
01:46:37,800 --> 01:46:41,024
I did what I thought
was right! I can go to my father...

1068
01:46:41,036 --> 01:46:44,479
...and explain everything gladly! 
Don't worry!

1069
01:46:44,480 --> 01:46:46,559
Alaeddin!

1070
01:46:46,760 --> 01:46:52,479
You made the biggest
mistake in your life by retreating!

1071
01:46:52,480 --> 01:46:55,959
You fled from that battlefield in fear. You!

1072
01:46:58,080 --> 01:46:59,639
You..

1073
01:47:02,680 --> 01:47:04,839
You are a coward, Alaeddin!

1074
01:47:07,999 --> 01:47:09,779
At least, I am...

1075
01:47:10,040 --> 01:47:13,839
...a coward who worries about
the lives of our men! But you are...

1076
01:47:14,560 --> 01:47:17,719
...an unaware man who drags his men to death!

1077
01:47:17,760 --> 01:47:19,399
You are nothing else!

1078
01:47:36,360 --> 01:47:40,159
-My Shahzade!
-Stop! Look around you!

1079
01:47:40,560 --> 01:47:45,759
This is battlefield! There is shame in
cowardice and honour in moving forward!

1080
01:47:45,760 --> 01:47:49,759
But if you are saying you
want to use ink with scholars...

1081
01:47:49,760 --> 01:47:53,679
...in the madrasah(school)
then Alaeddin...

1082
01:47:53,680 --> 01:47:55,359
...then you...

1083
01:47:59,560 --> 01:48:02,039
...have nothing to do in the battlefield!

1084
01:48:09,160 --> 01:48:11,639
You shouldn't have done this, Orhan Bey!

1085
01:48:13,000 --> 01:48:15,062
You shouldn't have done this!

1086
01:48:15,062 --> 01:48:18,719
-Done what, huh?
-Who are you, huh?

1087
01:48:18,720 --> 01:48:22,759
Who are you to hit me?
-Who are you?

1088
01:48:22,760 --> 01:48:24,359
Let me, Cerkutay Bey!

1089
01:48:24,360 --> 01:48:26,319
How could you leave your brother there?

1090
01:48:26,320 --> 01:48:30,319
How could you betray your Alps and martyrs?

1091
01:48:30,320 --> 01:48:33,119
Who are you to hit me?

1092
01:48:37,200 --> 01:48:41,919
This is only the beginning! We will
celebrate many more victories together!

1093
01:48:42,960 --> 01:48:47,919
Never forget that the greatest
defeats come while celebrating victory.

1094
01:48:50,240 --> 01:48:51,519
Don't talk like that.

1095
01:48:54,600 --> 01:48:56,239
Commander Gladius!

1096
01:49:00,440 --> 01:49:01,039
Hristo

1097
01:49:01,160 --> 01:49:04,719
I went to meet the troops that
will come to Bursa as you ordered.

1098
01:49:04,880 --> 01:49:05,959
Good.

1099
01:49:13,960 --> 01:49:15,719
Where is my army, Hristo?

1100
01:49:16,160 --> 01:49:17,319
Osman.

1101
01:49:18,600 --> 01:49:19,959
He raided the place.

1102
01:49:27,080 --> 01:49:28,199
Get out.

1103
01:49:38,160 --> 01:49:41,079
Never underestimate him.

1104
01:49:43,080 --> 01:49:44,119
Look.

1105
01:49:47,960 --> 01:49:50,559
He destroyed half of your army.

1106
01:49:51,560 --> 01:49:53,679
You defeated his sons.

1107
01:49:54,240 --> 01:49:55,879
Not Osman himself.

1108
01:49:57,080 --> 01:49:59,239
When Osman stands before me..

1109
01:49:59,640 --> 01:50:02,599
I promise you, he won't be as lucky as his sons.

1110
01:50:03,880 --> 01:50:08,239
Dying in the battlefield will be a gift for him.

1111
01:50:11,920 --> 01:50:13,199
Gladius..

1112
01:50:15,680 --> 01:50:20,079
I have waited for years to
make him feel the greatest pain.

1113
01:50:23,440 --> 01:50:24,879
It's time.

1114
01:50:34,760 --> 01:50:39,439
Those looks in your beautiful eyes...

1115
01:50:42,080 --> 01:50:44,399
I even pity your enemy.

1116
01:50:50,240 --> 01:50:51,599
Tell me.

1117
01:50:53,320 --> 01:50:55,159
What is your plan?

1118
01:50:55,600 --> 01:50:56,959
I will...

1119
01:50:59,520 --> 01:51:02,959
...kill Osman with his own child's hands.

1120
01:51:05,000 --> 01:51:08,919
He will die writhing in the pain of his soul...

1121
01:51:10,080 --> 01:51:12,559
...before the pain in his body.

1122
01:51:21,880 --> 01:51:25,519
Osman Bey won a victory!

1123
01:51:26,360 --> 01:51:27,679
Thanks.

1124
01:51:28,600 --> 01:51:31,479
Thank you, thank you.

1125
01:51:37,960 --> 01:51:41,359
-May your victory be blessed, my Bey.
-Thank you.

1126
01:51:41,520 --> 01:51:43,319
-Are you alright? 
-I am.

1127
01:52:04,280 --> 01:52:06,919
Orhan... Are you injured?

1128
01:52:12,240 --> 01:52:16,039
My Bey.

1129
01:52:17,040 --> 01:52:21,919
My sons... Are you alright?

1130
01:52:30,280 --> 01:52:31,719
What happened?

1131
01:52:33,600 --> 01:52:35,279
What happened at the outpost?

1132
01:52:39,400 --> 01:52:41,349
We were defeated, my Bey.

1133
01:52:43,480 --> 01:52:44,679
My Bey...

1134
01:52:45,040 --> 01:52:50,319
Villager Nicos who came to our tribe and
informed us about our Alps' situation...

1135
01:52:51,720 --> 01:52:54,439
...was the Byzantium Commander Gladius.

1136
01:52:59,880 --> 01:53:01,359
That dastard...

1137
01:53:02,880 --> 01:53:05,199
That dastard tricked us, my Bey.

1138
01:53:09,720 --> 01:53:11,279
And Alaeddin...

1139
01:53:16,080 --> 01:53:17,999
...left us there..

1140
01:53:19,000 --> 01:53:21,039
...and retreated.

1141
01:53:24,000 --> 01:53:27,759
-Patience, patience.
Because of Alaeddin..

1142
01:53:28,920 --> 01:53:31,799
...we returned to the tribe with defeat, my Bey.

1143
01:53:33,680 --> 01:53:35,039
Orhan Bey...

1144
01:53:35,680 --> 01:53:37,399
Do you think you are the only...

1145
01:53:37,720 --> 01:53:40,719
...commander of these valiants, huh?
-Alaeddin!

1146
01:53:41,880 --> 01:53:43,079
Bala.

1147
01:53:45,640 --> 01:53:49,119
If we hadn't retreated, we would
have been destroyed, my Bey.

1148
01:53:49,760 --> 01:53:50,839
But...

1149
01:53:51,280 --> 01:53:54,639
Orhan Bey's ambition
blinded him -When have we...

1150
01:53:55,120 --> 01:53:58,839
When have we run away from shahada, Alaeddin?

1151
01:54:00,760 --> 01:54:01,879
My Bey!

1152
01:54:02,520 --> 01:54:06,199
When did we run away from
shahada? We left Yusuf...

1153
01:54:06,280 --> 01:54:09,719
...our Alps, our martyrs behind us...

1154
01:54:09,720 --> 01:54:12,079
...and returned to our tribe with empty hands.

1155
01:54:12,080 --> 01:54:16,159
Now tell me Alaeddin Bey! Isn't what you did...

1156
01:54:16,160 --> 01:54:18,399
...isn't what you did shameful, huh?

1157
01:54:18,400 --> 01:54:21,199
My men burned alive there today!

1158
01:54:21,320 --> 01:54:25,559
The biggest shame for Beys is to
drag their men to death knowingly!

1159
01:54:25,560 --> 01:54:28,719
What are you saying?
-Are you going to teach me how to be a Bey?

1160
01:54:28,720 --> 01:54:32,519
Are you going to teach me how
to be a Bey? Know your limits!

1161
01:54:34,080 --> 01:54:35,279
Enough!

1162
01:54:48,080 --> 01:54:50,079
Your tongues became swords!

1163
01:54:50,280 --> 01:54:52,079
And you are hitting each other!

1164
01:55:02,000 --> 01:55:05,479
We don't even need enemies
when we have you two right now!

1165
01:55:39,920 --> 01:55:41,159
Yusuf...

1166
01:55:47,120 --> 01:55:48,279
My valiant...

1167
01:56:06,280 --> 01:56:08,039
He left a note, my Bey.

1168
01:56:17,760 --> 01:56:19,559
Your children are not...

1169
01:56:20,840 --> 01:56:22,839
...strong enough against me, Osman.

1170
01:56:23,360 --> 01:56:24,559
I am...

1171
01:56:25,360 --> 01:56:26,919
...waiting for you.

1172
01:56:29,680 --> 01:56:31,119
Gladius.

1173
01:56:34,120 --> 01:56:35,559
Do you see it now?

1174
01:56:35,840 --> 01:56:38,879
This is the end of the way you lead! See it!

1175
01:56:39,680 --> 01:56:41,199
Alaeddin!

1176
01:56:41,720 --> 01:56:44,039
Have some respect for the body here!

1177
01:56:51,280 --> 01:56:52,959
Get lost!

1178
01:56:55,720 --> 01:56:56,879
Get lost!

1179
01:57:27,040 --> 01:57:30,959
Don't you have a bit of shame, Alaeddin?

1180
01:57:31,640 --> 01:57:33,519
After all the things you did...

1181
01:57:34,080 --> 01:57:39,599
...will you come and sit at
the same table with my father?

1182
01:57:41,920 --> 01:57:43,279
Shame suits you...

1183
01:57:44,480 --> 01:57:46,359
...honour suits me.

1184
01:57:47,080 --> 01:57:50,799
I am always proud. -Is that so?

1185
01:57:52,320 --> 01:57:56,239
You left our martyrs in the
battlefield and ran away...

1186
01:57:56,280 --> 01:58:00,639
..and you will talk about honour
and pride before me here, huh?

1187
01:58:05,840 --> 01:58:07,319
Orhan Bey...

1188
01:58:09,000 --> 01:58:11,239
Watch your words.

1189
01:58:13,960 --> 01:58:16,839
Alaeddin... My father is
waiting for us, Alaeddin.

1190
01:58:20,640 --> 01:58:24,999
This situation makes me worried.
The conflict between Shahzades...

1191
01:58:25,120 --> 01:58:30,039
...overshadow our unity.
What will happen now, Beys?

1192
01:58:31,080 --> 01:58:35,079
My Osman Bey will calm them
down to bring peace, Aykurt.

1193
01:58:35,760 --> 01:58:37,359
God willing.

1194
01:58:43,040 --> 01:58:44,639
Let's not keep them waiting.

1195
01:58:46,160 --> 01:58:47,799
Come on Alaeddin.

1196
01:59:17,600 --> 01:59:19,999
Remove those two plates from the table.

1197
01:59:36,320 --> 01:59:37,399
My Bey.

1198
01:59:37,880 --> 01:59:40,519
I am telling you to take them away, Ulgen!

1199
01:59:40,920 --> 01:59:44,079
There is no place for those
two plates on this table!

1200
02:00:10,680 --> 02:00:13,439
No matter how many mistakes a child makes...

1201
02:00:13,680 --> 02:00:16,959
...there is always a place
for them at their father's table.

1202
02:00:17,360 --> 02:00:18,879
Don't, my Bey.

1203
02:00:20,000 --> 02:00:22,239
Don't, father.

1204
02:00:22,920 --> 02:00:26,919
I set this table for us to unite.

1205
02:00:27,640 --> 02:00:28,839
This place...

1206
02:00:30,200 --> 02:00:33,639
...is the most important
place for our family and state.

1207
02:00:35,840 --> 02:00:37,319
Those who shake it..

1208
02:00:37,720 --> 02:00:39,959
...those who bring destruction here...

1209
02:00:43,040 --> 02:00:45,439
...will not be let in this tent.

1210
02:01:02,440 --> 02:01:04,199
Daughters, you sit.

1211
02:01:15,720 --> 02:01:18,679
Those who have no place here know who they are.

1212
02:01:43,080 --> 02:01:46,519
What will happen now? How can we be separate?

1213
02:01:47,840 --> 02:01:51,519
We thought Halime would come
and that we would all be together...

1214
02:01:51,640 --> 02:01:57,119
Now this happened. We are losing each other.
-This matter will not be talked about today.

1215
02:01:59,600 --> 02:02:02,759
Ulgen. Come on, my daughter.
Put the meals on the plates.

1216
02:02:06,520 --> 02:02:08,079
Enjoy.

1217
02:02:17,880 --> 02:02:22,679
Do you like the result of your actions
Alaeddin? We were sent away...

1218
02:02:22,920 --> 02:02:26,279
...from my father's peaceful table.
-Enough.

1219
02:02:27,040 --> 02:02:29,999
We are in this situation
because of our ambition.

1220
02:02:30,960 --> 02:02:35,839
Even if you hit me once, even if you hit me for
a thousand times, the truth will not change.

1221
02:02:37,880 --> 02:02:39,599
And you are..

1222
02:02:45,320 --> 02:02:47,439
You are accusing me then.

1223
02:02:48,760 --> 02:02:50,519
Tell me Alaeddin.

1224
02:02:51,680 --> 02:02:54,639
Was I the one who left his brother...

1225
02:02:55,080 --> 02:02:58,839
...and martyrs in the battlefield?

1226
02:03:00,960 --> 02:03:02,359
Alaeddin..

1227
02:03:02,880 --> 02:03:04,679
...in that battlefield...

1228
02:03:05,440 --> 02:03:07,839
..because of your retreat..

1229
02:03:11,280 --> 02:03:14,159
...all our Alps were going to die.

1230
02:03:15,720 --> 02:03:17,119
Orhan Bey...

1231
02:03:18,320 --> 02:03:21,839
-Watch your words.
-I say this because I know the truth.

1232
02:03:21,840 --> 02:03:26,719
I am telling you the truth! And the truth
is, you ran away from that battlefield...

1233
02:03:28,800 --> 02:03:31,159
...because you were afraid, Alaeddin.

1234
02:03:32,640 --> 02:03:33,999
You should be thankful.

1235
02:03:40,120 --> 02:03:41,999
You should thank our father.

1236
02:03:45,320 --> 02:03:47,239
I am ignoring these words.

1237
02:03:48,240 --> 02:03:49,679
For now.

1238
02:04:07,600 --> 02:04:10,879
Are you happy with what you've done, brother?

1239
02:04:11,600 --> 02:04:12,639
Huh?

1240
02:04:13,160 --> 02:04:15,199
There is no unity in the tribe.

1241
02:04:15,800 --> 02:04:17,519
We could not take our martyrs.

1242
02:04:19,320 --> 02:04:22,519
How will we clean this dark stain, Cerkutay?

1243
02:04:24,800 --> 02:04:26,119
What was I supposed to do?

1244
02:04:27,960 --> 02:04:30,719
What? Would you not use your mind...

1245
02:04:30,760 --> 02:04:35,399
...and watch everyone become
martyrs while fighting for no reason?

1246
02:04:36,280 --> 02:04:39,279
No one would have come back to the tribe then.

1247
02:04:39,840 --> 02:04:44,679
At least, we would've died with our honour.
We would have been buried with honour.

1248
02:04:45,080 --> 02:04:47,719
We wouldn't be sitting here in embarrassment.

1249
02:04:49,760 --> 02:04:51,039
Brother..

1250
02:04:51,640 --> 02:04:53,479
If we died, we would be martyrs.

1251
02:04:54,280 --> 02:04:56,159
Now thanks to you...

1252
02:04:56,520 --> 02:04:59,519
...we are just a disgrace, Cerkutay.

1253
02:05:01,720 --> 02:05:03,199
Alaeddin Bey...

1254
02:05:04,040 --> 02:05:09,639
...is right. He did the
best thing by retreating.

1255
02:05:10,760 --> 02:05:12,119
Orhan Bey...

1256
02:05:13,640 --> 02:05:17,679
Orhan Bey was defeated by his
ambition. He shed brothers' blood.

1257
02:05:18,920 --> 02:05:20,119
And you..

1258
02:05:20,960 --> 02:05:22,839
Boran..

1259
02:05:23,440 --> 02:05:26,187
You should know what your
words can mean or else...

1260
02:05:26,199 --> 02:05:27,119
Or else?

1261
02:05:30,760 --> 02:05:33,999
Or else what, Cerkutay? What brother?

1262
02:05:34,640 --> 02:05:36,759
Or else, brother? What will happen?

1263
02:05:37,600 --> 02:05:39,239
Cerkutay Bey!

1264
02:05:40,320 --> 02:05:44,359
Boran Bey... Calm down.

1265
02:05:45,920 --> 02:05:47,359
Please, my Beys.

1266
02:05:47,640 --> 02:05:51,359
What are you doing? Does this suit you?

1267
02:05:57,920 --> 02:05:59,599
Don't, Beys.

1268
02:06:00,480 --> 02:06:02,999
Sow the wind, reap the whirlwind.

1269
02:06:03,480 --> 02:06:06,519
You are giving the infidels what they want.

1270
02:06:08,040 --> 02:06:10,279
If we look for separation...

1271
02:06:10,920 --> 02:06:13,519
...we will be destroyed and die out.

1272
02:06:13,880 --> 02:06:16,239
Koca Bey is right, brothers.

1273
02:06:16,360 --> 02:06:19,319
Let's kill infidels instead
of hurting each other.

1274
02:06:20,520 --> 02:06:27,119
Whenever the lineage of Oghuz
separated, they died. Union is strength.

1275
02:06:29,520 --> 02:06:31,879
Osman Bey is with you.

1276
02:06:32,280 --> 02:06:36,839
Do not let him down.
When the right time comes...

1277
02:06:36,840 --> 02:06:39,719
...he will tell you what is right.

1278
02:06:40,520 --> 02:06:43,679
Now is time to leave.

1279
02:06:44,320 --> 02:06:45,519
Go now.

1280
02:06:46,320 --> 02:06:48,239
Have a good night.

1281
02:07:21,640 --> 02:07:23,839
What is it about, Koca Bey?

1282
02:07:24,160 --> 02:07:26,519
It's not an important issue, my Bey.

1283
02:07:27,400 --> 02:07:30,279
Both sides are right in their own way.

1284
02:07:31,320 --> 02:07:32,359
Well..

1285
02:07:32,640 --> 02:07:35,279
They are fighting for the state in the end.

1286
02:07:35,640 --> 02:07:39,599
When the time comes,
their ambition will go away.

1287
02:07:40,520 --> 02:07:41,599
No.

1288
02:07:43,600 --> 02:07:45,999
There must be an issue.

1289
02:07:48,040 --> 02:07:49,759
Right, Koca Bey?

1290
02:07:52,560 --> 02:07:53,959
We need union...

1291
02:07:55,560 --> 02:07:57,039
...for the state.

1292
02:07:57,840 --> 02:07:59,359
If there is duality...

1293
02:08:01,880 --> 02:08:03,959
this will destroy the state

1294
02:08:10,920 --> 02:08:13,479
I know what to do to them.

1295
02:08:23,120 --> 02:08:24,559
Very beautiful.

1296
02:08:25,320 --> 02:08:27,559
She resembles your youth.

1297
02:08:28,160 --> 02:08:29,199
Right?

1298
02:08:34,320 --> 02:08:36,559
What are you doing here?

1299
02:08:37,800 --> 02:08:40,759
Do you remember? It's in the past but...

1300
02:08:40,760 --> 02:08:43,079
...when I was younger..
-Lower your voice.

1301
02:08:43,080 --> 02:08:45,559
I always wanted to come
to you before I left for battles.

1302
02:08:45,560 --> 02:08:49,959
I told you to lower your voice.
To see you for one last time. -Lower...

1303
02:08:57,440 --> 02:08:59,599
I don't want her to wake up.

1304
02:09:06,400 --> 02:09:08,759
And I don't want you to go to Osman.

1305
02:09:10,880 --> 02:09:12,399
There is no need for this.

1306
02:09:13,120 --> 02:09:14,639
Send a messenger.

1307
02:09:14,960 --> 02:09:17,759
Or something bad might
happen to you at the tribe.

1308
02:09:17,960 --> 02:09:20,879
I should do this to convince them.

1309
02:09:23,000 --> 02:09:25,879
Mongols are coming Gladius.

1310
02:09:26,440 --> 02:09:29,479
I have no other choice than talking to Osman.

1311
02:09:30,920 --> 02:09:32,919
Osman will trust you.

1312
02:09:33,440 --> 02:09:34,839
He will believe you.

1313
02:09:43,680 --> 02:09:45,039
He will trust me.

1314
02:10:11,080 --> 02:10:14,559
My Bey, you haven't slept all night.

1315
02:10:14,760 --> 02:10:17,399
This is the first time I
am seeing you like this.

1316
02:10:17,560 --> 02:10:23,599
Tell me... What are you thinking of doing?
-Whoever does harm to the...

1317
02:10:25,040 --> 02:10:28,399
...unity and strength of our state...

1318
02:10:30,520 --> 02:10:33,959
...even if they are my
children, I will never allow this.

1319
02:10:34,680 --> 02:10:39,119
No. I won't.

1320
02:10:40,760 --> 02:10:41,919
Boran!

1321
02:10:46,800 --> 02:10:49,999
Yes my Bey.
-Tell Orhan and Alaeddin to come here.

1322
02:10:50,280 --> 02:10:51,799
As you order my Bey.

1323
02:10:59,000 --> 02:11:00,559
My Alaeddin Ali..

1324
02:11:01,760 --> 02:11:04,399
Everyone knows why you did this.

1325
02:11:05,240 --> 02:11:09,239
You have prevented a great disaster
that was about to happen, Alaeddin.

1326
02:11:09,240 --> 02:11:10,559
I have.

1327
02:11:12,680 --> 02:11:14,439
I have, yes.

1328
02:11:17,960 --> 02:11:20,439
I left my martyr Alps behind, Gonca.

1329
02:11:20,560 --> 02:11:22,799
Now how are we going to look at their...

1330
02:11:23,040 --> 02:11:25,679
...mothers' and children's faces?

1331
02:11:26,240 --> 02:11:27,399
Alaeddin..

1332
02:11:28,960 --> 02:11:30,879
But with what you did...

1333
02:11:31,120 --> 02:11:34,279
...many Alps came back to their families.

1334
02:11:35,640 --> 02:11:38,919
I see my father like this
for the first time, Gonca.

1335
02:11:40,360 --> 02:11:46,759
I would enter the enemy's nest
alone rather than lose his trust.

1336
02:11:47,200 --> 02:11:50,519
I know. I know, of course.

1337
02:11:51,520 --> 02:11:53,759
Everyone knows this, Alaeddin.

1338
02:11:54,720 --> 02:11:56,559
You did not make a mistake.

1339
02:11:57,520 --> 02:11:59,799
It was Orhan Bey who was defeated...

1340
02:12:00,080 --> 02:12:03,679
...by his anger and who
hit you before all those Alps.

1341
02:12:04,280 --> 02:12:06,599
Can I come in, my Shahzade?

1342
02:12:09,440 --> 02:12:11,079
Come in, Aykurt.

1343
02:12:11,840 --> 02:12:15,879
-Peace be upon you. Peace be upon you too.
-My Shahzade.

1344
02:12:15,920 --> 02:12:18,319
Osman Bey wants to see you in his tent.

1345
02:12:27,080 --> 02:12:30,439
We lost our Alps and our men.

1346
02:12:30,440 --> 02:12:34,279
We were about to gain a
victory, but we lost because of him.

1347
02:12:34,280 --> 02:12:37,879
Because of the duality he
caused, for the first time in my life...

1348
02:12:37,880 --> 02:12:39,599
...I was sent away from...

1349
02:12:40,640 --> 02:12:42,719
...my father's love and table.

1350
02:12:44,120 --> 02:12:46,919
What can I say now? Huh?

1351
02:12:47,320 --> 02:12:49,519
When my own brother...

1352
02:12:51,720 --> 02:12:53,679
When my own brother...

1353
02:12:54,880 --> 02:12:57,159
...did this to me..

1354
02:12:58,400 --> 02:13:00,639
...who am I going to trust, Holofira?

1355
02:13:02,240 --> 02:13:04,919
Can I come in, my Shahzade?

1356
02:13:09,040 --> 02:13:10,679
Come in Cerkutay.

1357
02:13:21,760 --> 02:13:23,119
My Shahzade.

1358
02:13:24,040 --> 02:13:26,039
Osman Bey is waiting for you.

1359
02:13:41,760 --> 02:13:44,399
-You called us, my Bey.
-Stop there!

1360
02:13:58,680 --> 02:14:00,679
You are not looking into the eyes...

1361
02:14:04,080 --> 02:14:05,839
...of your father.

1362
02:14:09,720 --> 02:14:12,159
This is the Bey of the state, Osman Bey.

1363
02:14:19,960 --> 02:14:23,439
Look what Orhan Bey caused
with what he did, Holofira.

1364
02:14:24,480 --> 02:14:25,759
You should know that...

1365
02:14:26,520 --> 02:14:28,559
...this fire will burn the tribe down.

1366
02:14:29,480 --> 02:14:33,639
When it is Alaeddin Bey who went against
his brother's orders and lost his trust...

1367
02:14:33,640 --> 02:14:37,039
..how can you accuse Orhan?
-Lost his trust?

1368
02:14:38,080 --> 02:14:40,359
Which trust are you talking about Hatun?

1369
02:14:40,360 --> 02:14:43,599
Can trust that is ruined at the
first difficulty be called trust?

1370
02:14:43,640 --> 02:14:46,719
Apparently, Orhan Bey is
ready to give up on his brother.

1371
02:14:46,720 --> 02:14:48,559
And this is his excuse.

1372
02:14:48,560 --> 02:14:52,239
You are the one who is looking for
an excuse and growing the fire, Gonca.

1373
02:14:52,240 --> 02:14:54,479
Orhan only cares about his cause.

1374
02:14:55,440 --> 02:14:59,039
Those who care about the cause
fight against infidels, Holofira.

1375
02:14:59,040 --> 02:15:03,039
They don't fight against their brothers.
Who are you trying to fool, huh?

1376
02:15:04,000 --> 02:15:05,559
But know this..

1377
02:15:06,400 --> 02:15:08,959
If Alaeddin gets hurt...

1378
02:15:10,880 --> 02:15:12,639
..I will hurt others even more.

1379
02:15:15,280 --> 02:15:17,559
Are you threatening me, Gonca?

1380
02:15:18,640 --> 02:15:22,879
I can burn the whole world for Orhan.

1381
02:15:23,680 --> 02:15:25,719
And I know this well that...

1382
02:15:27,240 --> 02:15:29,639
...even if you are trying to cause disorder...

1383
02:15:30,400 --> 02:15:34,599
...Orhan can make all infidels kneel
to protect Alaeddin from getting hurt.

1384
02:15:35,000 --> 02:15:36,319
He can.

1385
02:15:40,320 --> 02:15:43,959
Is that why he yelled at Alaeddin,
humiliated him before Alps...

1386
02:15:43,960 --> 02:15:47,679
...and told him to go back to mad rasa, huh?

1387
02:15:47,680 --> 02:15:49,879
Battlefield is different, Gonca!

1388
02:15:49,880 --> 02:15:52,119
I grew up in that field, Holofira!

1389
02:15:52,400 --> 02:15:54,839
I know the battlefield better than you!

1390
02:15:54,920 --> 02:15:59,919
But in the battlefield, we shed
enemies' blood, not brothers' blood!

1391
02:16:05,920 --> 02:16:07,079
What happened?

1392
02:16:08,210 --> 02:16:09,799
Didn't you know?

1393
02:16:11,480 --> 02:16:16,159
Did Orhan Bey not tell you that
he hit Alaeddin before all the Alps?

1394
02:16:21,360 --> 02:16:22,559
He did not.

1395
02:16:38,120 --> 02:16:44,839
I could not teach you anything as your father.

1396
02:16:45,680 --> 02:16:47,039
Nothing.

1397
02:16:48,400 --> 02:16:49,919
If someone...

1398
02:16:52,080 --> 02:16:54,039
...came to me and told me that..

1399
02:16:55,200 --> 02:16:57,799
...my children would fight...

1400
02:16:59,520 --> 02:17:01,839
..I would never believe this.

1401
02:17:06,879 --> 02:17:09,397
I would never believe this.

1402
02:17:10,240 --> 02:17:11,558
Never.

1403
02:17:13,120 --> 02:17:14,799
Shame on you..

1404
02:17:15,280 --> 02:17:19,439
Shame on you. Shame on you.. Shame on you..

1405
02:17:23,480 --> 02:17:25,119
Now...

1406
02:17:27,320 --> 02:17:31,558
You are both talking to the
ruler of the state, Osman Bey.

1407
02:17:32,000 --> 02:17:34,271
What is your problem? Tell me!

1408
02:17:34,282 --> 02:17:36,718
My Bey, we lost in a battle...

1409
02:17:36,718 --> 02:17:40,638
...when we were about to gain
a victory. That's why I am angry.

1410
02:17:42,120 --> 02:17:45,439
Orhan Bey is not telling
you all the details, my Bey.

1411
02:17:45,959 --> 02:17:49,159
We were caught unaware, and
we were in a difficult position.

1412
02:17:49,160 --> 02:17:52,039
No one could know if we
were going to win or lose.

1413
02:17:52,040 --> 02:17:54,439
We got into many battles until this day, my Bey.

1414
02:17:54,440 --> 02:17:57,279
With Allah's permission,
we survived in all of them.

1415
02:17:57,280 --> 02:18:00,919
Of course, we could not defeat our
enemies in all of them. But my Bey...

1416
02:18:00,920 --> 02:18:02,638
...when have we ever...

1417
02:18:03,240 --> 02:18:05,999
...left our men behind and run away?

1418
02:18:06,600 --> 02:18:08,199
I did not run away!

1419
02:18:10,799 --> 02:18:14,119
I retreated by following our morals. But you...

1420
02:18:14,480 --> 02:18:16,638
...you let your ambition...
-Shut up!

1421
02:18:19,280 --> 02:18:21,519
You are still nursing your grudge!

1422
02:18:25,320 --> 02:18:26,718
Look at me.

1423
02:18:30,879 --> 02:18:32,919
Listen to me carefully.

1424
02:18:35,400 --> 02:18:36,799
Whoever tries..

1425
02:18:38,200 --> 02:18:41,199
...to cause disorder and duality in my state...

1426
02:18:44,160 --> 02:18:46,199
I will never allow them.

1427
02:18:48,520 --> 02:18:50,397
Whoever tries to separate...

1428
02:18:50,680 --> 02:18:53,879
...my banner and my nation...

1429
02:18:56,520 --> 02:19:04,317
I will never allow them. Even
if they are my own children.

1430
02:19:09,040 --> 02:19:11,599
...I am Osman Bey.

1431
02:19:12,000 --> 02:19:14,759
I will never let this happen!

1432
02:19:16,718 --> 02:19:18,718
We need justice for the state!

1433
02:19:19,638 --> 02:19:21,839
We need unity for the state!

1434
02:19:24,558 --> 02:19:26,477
You should know.

1435
02:19:28,160 --> 02:19:29,919
In this struggle...

1436
02:19:31,638 --> 02:19:34,599
...whoever stands in my way...

1437
02:19:35,760 --> 02:19:37,959
...I will never allow them to move.

1438
02:19:46,920 --> 02:19:48,239
Therefore..

1439
02:19:50,080 --> 02:19:52,079
..you will either unite...

1440
02:19:52,920 --> 02:19:54,159
...or...

1441
02:19:55,240 --> 02:19:56,519
...I will...

1442
02:19:56,920 --> 02:19:59,279
...walk on this path without you.

1443
02:20:03,800 --> 02:20:04,919
Boran.

1444
02:20:10,160 --> 02:20:11,559
Yes my Bey.

1445
02:20:12,000 --> 02:20:13,439
Tell the Alps to get ready.

1446
02:20:15,240 --> 02:20:17,199
We will go and take our martyrs.

1447
02:20:18,040 --> 02:20:19,439
As you order my Bey.

1448
02:20:22,840 --> 02:20:24,239
No.

1449
02:20:24,960 --> 02:20:26,799
You will not come.

1450
02:20:31,120 --> 02:20:33,079
My sword is enough for me.

1451
02:20:40,800 --> 02:20:44,599
You snake!

1452
02:21:08,560 --> 02:21:10,039
Sofia.

1453
02:21:10,840 --> 02:21:12,279
What is happening?

1454
02:21:15,480 --> 02:21:16,879
You snake..

1455
02:21:23,040 --> 02:21:24,413
How could she come here?

1456
02:21:24,425 --> 02:21:26,559
What is she trying
to do this time?

1457
02:21:26,800 --> 02:21:30,999
She is approaching her death.

1458
02:21:36,840 --> 02:21:37,999
Sofia.

1459
02:21:38,480 --> 02:21:41,199
You demon! How could
you come to this tribe, huh?

1460
02:21:41,280 --> 02:21:44,297
Don't you know that I
won't let you survive here?

1461
02:21:44,309 --> 02:21:45,319
Bala!

1462
02:21:45,320 --> 02:21:48,639
Today, there will be no bloodshed. No death.

1463
02:21:49,760 --> 02:21:53,559
-There will be peace. 
-Attention!

1464
02:21:55,040 --> 02:21:56,439
Osman Bey!

1465
02:22:03,400 --> 02:22:04,599
What is it?

1466
02:22:05,800 --> 02:22:08,697
Did you come to your own
death with your own feet?

1467
02:22:08,709 --> 02:22:09,679
No.

1468
02:22:09,720 --> 02:22:12,359
I am too young to die.

1469
02:22:12,680 --> 02:22:13,839
Today...

1470
02:22:14,200 --> 02:22:16,159
...I am here on behalf of Byzantium.

1471
02:22:17,360 --> 02:22:21,039
-For an alliance.
-Are we going to make an alliance with you?

1472
02:22:26,120 --> 02:22:28,759
We have a common enemy, Osman.

1473
02:22:33,040 --> 02:22:34,479
Olcaytu.

1474
02:22:36,360 --> 02:22:39,759
If Olcaytu takes your
lands, he will also take Bursa.

1475
02:22:42,520 --> 02:22:45,119
We are on the same side today.

1476
02:22:53,080 --> 02:22:55,639
The offer of the Mongol envoy.

1477
02:23:06,760 --> 02:23:07,999
Look.

1478
02:23:09,480 --> 02:23:10,639
Look carefully.

1479
02:23:17,440 --> 02:23:19,839
An alliance is your only option.

1480
02:23:22,760 --> 02:23:24,799
Olcaytu is coming.

1481
02:23:25,080 --> 02:23:26,439
Osman Bey.

1482
02:23:27,600 --> 02:23:29,679
This means destruction.

1483
02:23:32,080 --> 02:23:36,839
I would neither trust nor ally...

1484
02:23:38,800 --> 02:23:44,119
...with an executioner like you, who brought...

1485
02:23:49,240 --> 02:23:51,399
...unimaginable suffering to my family...

1486
02:23:55,920 --> 02:23:57,959
...and kidnapped my child.

1487
02:24:02,520 --> 02:24:05,679
Look! Taking your life is halal to me!

1488
02:24:06,400 --> 02:24:07,679
I can kill you here!

1489
02:24:10,720 --> 02:24:15,679
And then I can attack Olcaytu with all my power.

1490
02:24:16,600 --> 02:24:18,759
And I will also take Bursa for which...

1491
02:24:18,800 --> 02:24:25,799
...you offer peace to your enemy!

1492
02:24:26,080 --> 02:24:29,879
You still don't believe me, huh?

1493
02:24:30,080 --> 02:24:33,719
From now on, the only agreement we'll make is...

1494
02:24:33,800 --> 02:24:37,279
...to take your life without pain,
Sofia. Expect nothing else from us.

1495
02:24:39,040 --> 02:24:40,319
Alright.

1496
02:24:43,960 --> 02:24:45,159
Alright.

1497
02:24:48,760 --> 02:24:51,479
I will convince you of my sincerity.

1498
02:24:54,280 --> 02:24:57,759
You stole my future from me Osman Bey.

1499
02:24:59,400 --> 02:25:02,079
In return for my unborn children...

1500
02:25:03,520 --> 02:25:05,639
...and the dreams...

1501
02:25:06,520 --> 02:25:08,639
..you took from me..

1502
02:25:09,560 --> 02:25:11,759
..I stole Halime from you.

1503
02:25:13,320 --> 02:25:14,759
We are even.

1504
02:25:15,920 --> 02:25:17,199
Now...

1505
02:25:19,760 --> 02:25:24,289
I will give you my most precious one
whom I raised with my own hands...

1506
02:25:29,480 --> 02:25:32,119
...Halime.

1507
02:25:32,600 --> 02:25:33,879
Sofia..

1508
02:25:34,160 --> 02:25:35,578
You are playing games again!

1509
02:25:35,590 --> 02:25:38,399
I told you, I am not playing
a game this time, Bala!

1510
02:25:38,720 --> 02:25:40,639
Giving her to you...

1511
02:25:42,080 --> 02:25:46,879
...is as painful as seeing Kayi flag in Bursa!

1512
02:25:47,400 --> 02:25:52,879
-Where is Halime?!
-Her name is not Halime! I named her Poena!

1513
02:25:54,920 --> 02:25:56,559
And she is in Bursa now.

1514
02:26:01,320 --> 02:26:04,319
And this time I am really telling you the truth.

1515
02:26:06,040 --> 02:26:07,159
Now..

1516
02:26:08,920 --> 02:26:10,439
...the decision is yours.

1517
02:26:11,560 --> 02:26:13,079
If you still..

1518
02:26:14,480 --> 02:26:20,479
...want your daughter back who hates Turks...

1519
02:26:20,480 --> 02:26:22,159
...I have only one condition.

1520
02:26:25,280 --> 02:26:27,199
Alliance against Mongols.